     "question": "For code paper alignment: methodology matches code, is there affirmative evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence?",
     "reason": "Identify evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence. A missing artifact, unrun experiment, weak result, or unproven claim alone is insufficient.",
     "judge_reason": "The reported ANI-1x motif-labeling method materially contradicts the executed implementation. Methods says the grammar is evaluated on each molecule's lowest-energy conformation c0. After merging graph classes by canonical SMILES, the transfer code instead uses the first encountered class's labels. Saved records show that this is not the minimum-energy class for 9,149 of 30,609 molecules; at least one atlas label differs from the saved minimum-energy-class labels for 5,444 molecules. This is a substantive method-description contradiction, independent of intent.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/sections/methods.tex:25: 'the grammar is evaluated on each molecule's lowest-energy conformation c_0.'",
      "proposal/code/ani1x_transfer.py:83–103 merges classes and assigns rep_class using setdefault; lines 188–189 use that first class's motif labels. Lines 116–125 separately select the actual minimum for energy referencing.",
      "proposal/code/ani1x_extract.py:107–118 orders graph classes by their hash keys and sorts energies only within each class.",
      "Read-only comparison of proposal/cache/ani1x_le9.npz fields mol/E_kcal with proposal/cache/ani1x_le9_molecules.pkl establishes the 9,149 and 5,444 counts.",
      "proposal/logs/ani1x/transfer_all_candidates.json reports G04 support of 5,460, exactly matching first-class labels; the saved labels of the minimum-energy classes give 3,627. All 68 reported motif counts match the first-class labeling."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "unresolved_reasons": [],
   "assessment_status": "fail",
   "failure_basis": [
    "detected_violation"
   ]
