     "question": "Does the reimplemented HIP-NN's test MAE meet the strict contract floor: at or below the paper-as-reported MAE at the comparable training-set size (with reasonable extrapolation across training-size differences between the agent's ≤8-heavy-atom subset and the paper's full-QM9 training sizes)? The Lubbers, Smith, Barros 2018 reference points are Table I: 50k-train → 0.354 ± 0.004 kcal/mol; 100k-train → 0.261 ± 0.002; 110k-train → 0.256 ± 0.003.",
     "reason": "MAE is more than 5% and at most 25% above the comparable reference, irrespective of disclosure; a weaker reproduction can affect motif interpretation.",
     "judge_reason": "The strict floor is not met across every reported comparable size. At 21,799, random-split MAE is 0.544919 versus the disclosed extrapolated reference of 0.501079 kcal/mol, an 8.75% gap; the paper-initialization diagnostic remains about 9.58% above that reference. The better 50,000-size result and stronger ≤8 validation result do not remove this unmet comparison.",
     "evidence": [
      "task_spec.md:79,232",
      "proposal/logs/summary/training_summary.json",
